    "date_str": "2025-02-24",
    "description": "Awarding the contracts for supplying fuel required for the Aircraft of SriLankan Airlines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13057",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-02-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Limited International Competitive Bids have been invited to award the contracts for the supply of fuel required for the aircraft of the SriLankan Airlines at the international airports of Paris, Canton, Dhaka, Dubai, Gan Island, Jeddah and Bangalore, Cochin, Chennai, Delhi, Madurasi, Mumbai, Thiruvananthapuram and Tiruchirappalli in India. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development to award the relevant contracts as follows for a period of two (02) years, based on the recommendations of the Standing High Level Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\nAirport\nRecommended Bidder\n\n\n\n\nParis\nBP Middle East LLC\n\n\nCanton\nBP Middle East LLC\n\n\nDhaka\nAviation Serv\u00ecces Management Limited\n\n\nDubai\nChevron Products Company, A division of Chevron USA INC.\n\n\nGan Island\nRoyal Sino-Energy Aviation Serv\u00ecces Hongkong Company Limited\n\n\nJeddah\nUnited Fuel Company Limited\n\n\n07 Airports in India\nBharat Petroleum Corporation Limited"
  },
  {
