    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-02-15",
    "description": "Long-Term management of maritime wrecks and underwater cultural heritage of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3889",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Shipwrecks are considered as the heritage of the nation, representing historical, cultural and archeological value and the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA) is the Government Institution responsible for the management, development and conservation of Aquatic Resources. Very old wrecks are a major attraction for underwater photographers, divers and tourists. On a proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, Cabinet approval was granted for the preparation of a long term broad based management plan for Sri Lanka's maritime wrecks and underwater cultural heritage, based on a thorough survey to be carried out by NARA and in association with the Ministries of Economic Development; Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development; Environment; and National Heritage."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-15-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-02-15",
    "description": "Bill to incorporate the institute of Applied Statistics, Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3888",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. Pavithra Wanniarachchi, Minister of Technology and Research, Cabinet approval was granted to present the Institute of Applied Statistics, Sri Lanka (Incorporation) Bill, prepared by the Legal Draftsman to be presented in Parliament.  The main objective of this Bill are as follows: \r\n\r\n*\tpromote and assist the advancement of Applied Statistics for the furtherance of research, development, education, training etc.;\r\n*\tundertake the preparation and publication of useful information pertaining to Applied Statistics by means of Seminars, Lectures and Articles to be published to foster the training of Research Workers;\r\n*\tundertake research work in this field; and\r\n*\tco-operative with governmental and non-governmental organizations and national and international institutes pertaining to activities in this field."
  },
