    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Amendment to the fine imposed under the Pesticide Control Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3875",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Provisions under this Act enable the control of Import, Packing, Labeling, Storing, Mixing, Transporting, Selling and Utilizing pesticides to ensure its proper management.   Since the existing fines for violation of provisions in the above Act have been imposed nearly three decades back and also due to the increase of environmental and health hazards caused due to handling of pesticides in an irresponsible manner, on a proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Yapa Abeywardhana, Minister of Agriculture, Cabinet approval was granted to increase the fine on an individual, from Rs.50,000/- to Rs.100,000/- and on a Body Corporate such as registered companies or corporations, from Rs.100,000/- to Rs.500,000/- and to present the relevant Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman in Parliament for approval. \r\n\r\n\tIt was also decided that an aggressive awareness campaign should be launched to educate farmers about the proper use of Agro chemicals and the disposal of empty containers in a non-hazardous manner."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Intake of  more foreign Students to Sri Lankan Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the present policy is to   reserve 0.5% of the proposed intake in each course of study for the benefit of foreign students. The proposal by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, Minister of Higher Education, to increase the intake of foreign students to the Sri Lankan Universities initially from 0.5% to 5% and later to 10% based on the success of the initial stage,without reducing the opportunities for local students, was approved by the Cabinet. This would not only gain additional foreign exchange to the country, but will also give wide publicity throughout the world for the quality of education in Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Indo-Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement (ISFTA) and Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3873",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the representatives of the two Governments which met in November 2010 in Colombo noted the significant progress made under the ISFTA and reaffirmed the understanding that it would be timely to build on this achievement through a more comprehensive framework of economic cooperation.  Accordingly, on a proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, Minister of Industry and Commerce, Cabinet approval was granted to appoint an Inter-Agency Committee to prepare a new draft framework for the purpose between India and Sri Lanka.  Views of the professionals and other stakeholders will also be entertained by this Committee."
  },
  {
